;TWO MOLECULES IN THE ASYMMETRIC UNIT ARE RELATED BY AN
APPROXIMATE TWO-FOLD AXIS.  THE TRANSFORMATION PRESENTED ON
*MTRIX* RECORDS BELOW WILL YIELD APPROXIMATE COORDINATES
FOR CHAINS *D* AND *E* WHEN APPLIED TO CHAINS *A* AND *B*,
RESPECTIVELY.

MOLECULE 1 : ALPHA CHAIN - RESIDUES  A   3 THROUGH A 182
           : BETA  CHAIN - RESIDUES  B   3 THROUGH B 190
           : PEPTIDE     - RESIDUES  C 306 THROUGH C 318
           : SUGARS      - RESIDUES  A 501, B 511, B 512,
                                     B 521
MOLECULE 2 : ALPHA CHAIN - RESIDUES  D   3 THROUGH D 182
           : BETA  CHAIN - RESIDUES  E   3 THROUGH E 190
           : PEPTIDE     - RESIDUES  F 306 THROUGH F 318
           : SUGARS      - RESIDUES  D 501, E 511, E 512,
                                     E 521
    WATERS : MOL1 + MOL2 - RESIDUES      1 THROUGH 153
;
